The magnetic field inside a toroid (ignoring fringe effects) is given by  

\[
B = \frac{\mu_0 N I}{2\pi r}
\]

where  

* \(N = 500\) turns  
* \(I = 4\;\text{A}\)  
* \(r = 15\ \text{cm}=0.15\ \text{m}\)  
* \(\mu_0 = 4\pi\times10^{-7}\ \text{H/m}\).

\[
B = \frac{(4\pi\times10^{-7})\,(500)(4)}{2\pi(0.15)}
